---
/**
 * GsmModelDiagram — the GSM data model, simplified and meaningful:
 * every GSM object is a Definition (stable identity); Ascriptions are its
 * governed, versioned snapshots; every Ascription is typed by an Archetype —
 * itself a Definition with Ascriptions; frameworks instantiate ascriptions
 * of every kind. The DNA grammar governs it all.
 */
---
<div class="gsmd" role="img" aria-label="Simplified GSM data model: every GSM object is a Definition; Ascriptions are its governed, versioned snapshots, lifecycle-managed; every Ascription is typed by an Archetype, itself a Definition; frameworks instantiate ascriptions of every kind — the DNA grammar is Directive, operationalized by Norm, bound by Ascription">
  <div class="gsmd-band gsmd-band--define">
    <span class="gsmd-band-label">Define</span>
    <div class="gsmd-box">
      <strong>Definition</strong>
      <span>The stable identity — <em>what something is</em>, bound to its subject. Every GSM object is a Definition, of one of the eight classes:</span>
    </div>
    <div class="gsmd-cols">
      <div class="gsmd-group">
        <span class="gsmd-group-label">the acting system</span>
        <div class="gsmd-chips">
          <span class="gsmd-chip">Structure</span>
          <span class="gsmd-chip">Mechanism</span>
          <span class="gsmd-chip">Effector</span>
          <span class="gsmd-chip">Receptor</span>
          <span class="gsmd-chip">Interaction</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="gsmd-group">
        <span class="gsmd-group-label">the governing intent</span>
        <div class="gsmd-chips">
          <span class="gsmd-chip gsmd-chip--gov" title="Strategic intent / objective">Directive<small>strategic intent</small></span>
          <span class="gsmd-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→ operationalized by →</span>
          <span class="gsmd-chip gsmd-chip--gov" title="Tactical, measurable constraint / objective">Norm<small>tactical, measurable constraint</small></span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="gsmd-group">
        <span class="gsmd-group-label">the typing</span>
        <div class="gsmd-chips">
          <span class="gsmd-chip">Archetype</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="gsmd-rel" aria-hidden="true">versioned &amp; governed as ↓</div>
  </div>

  <div class="gsmd-band gsmd-band--version">
    <span class="gsmd-band-label">Version</span>
    <div class="gsmd-box">
      <strong>Ascription</strong>
      <span>A governed <em>version / snapshot</em> of its Definition at a point in time — the Definition binds its Ascriptions to the subject; each approved Ascription gets the next version number.</span>
      <span class="gsmd-lifecycle"><code>DRAFT → PROPOSED → APPROVED → ACTIVE → DEPRECATED → RETIRED</code> — every transition is a validated state change with referee preconditions; retirement cascades follow dependent definitions; identity-bound properties never change across versions.</span>
    </div>
    <div class="gsmd-rel" aria-hidden="true">every Ascription is typed by ↓</div>
  </div>

  <div class="gsmd-band gsmd-band--type">
    <span class="gsmd-band-label">Type</span>
    <div class="gsmd-box">
      <strong>Archetype</strong>
      <span>The JSON Schema that types an Ascription and validates its content — meaning travels with the type. An Archetype is <em>itself a Definition with Ascriptions</em>, governed like everything else.</span>
    </div>
    <div class="gsmd-extend">
      <span class="gsmd-extend-label">frameworks instantiate ascriptions of every kind —</span>
      <span class="gsmd-chips gsmd-chips--inline">
        <span class="gsmd-chip gsmd-chip--fw">TOGAF</span>
        <span class="gsmd-chip gsmd-chip--fw">GDPR</span>
        <span class="gsmd-chip gsmd-chip--fw">NIS2</span>
        <span class="gsmd-chip gsmd-chip--fw">ISO 25000</span>
        <span class="gsmd-chip gsmd-chip--fw">HTTP</span>
        <span class="gsmd-chip gsmd-chip--fw">ITIP</span>
        <span class="gsmd-chip gsmd-chip--fw">…</span>
      </span>
      <span class="gsmd-extend-note">domain Archetypes that extend the base GSM types, and sourced Directives and Norms carrying the framework's normative content — all entering the model as governed ascriptions</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="gsmd-dna">
    <strong>The DNA grammar</strong> = <span class="gsmd-chip gsmd-chip--gov gsmd-chip--sm">Directive</span> + <span class="gsmd-chip gsmd-chip--gov gsmd-chip--sm">Norm</span> + <span class="gsmd-chip gsmd-chip--gov gsmd-chip--sm">Ascription</span> — strategic intent, operationalized into measurable constraints, versioned and bound under lifecycle governance.
  </p>
</div>

<style>
  .gsmd {
    margin-top: 1.75rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0;
  }
  .gsmd-band {
    position: relative;
    border: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--bg-soft);
    padding: 1.1rem 1.2rem 1.1rem 5.5rem;
  }
  .gsmd-band + .gsmd-band {
    margin-top: 2.1rem;
  }
  .gsmd-band-label {
    position: absolute;
    left: 1.2rem;
    top: 1.15rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .gsmd-box strong {
    display: block;
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .gsmd-box span {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 0.35rem;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    line-height: 1.45;
  }
  .gsmd-lifecycle {
    font-size: 0.8rem !important;
    color: var(--muted) !important;
  }
  .gsmd-extend {
    margin-top: 0.8rem;
    padding-top: 0.7rem;
    border-top: 1px dashed var(--line);
  }
  .gsmd-extend-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-right: 0.4rem;
  }
  .gsmd-extend-note {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 0.45rem;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.45;
  }
  .gsmd-rel {
    position: absolute;
    left: 50%;
    bottom: -1.75rem;
    transform: translateX(-50%);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    white-space: nowrap;
    z-index: 1;
  }
  .gsmd-cols {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 1.4fr 0.6fr;
    gap: 1.4rem;
    margin-top: 0.85rem;
  }
  .gsmd-group-label {
    display: block;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 0.55rem;
  }
  .gsmd-chips {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.45rem;
  }
  .gsmd-chips--inline {
    display: inline-flex;
  }
  .gsmd-chip {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    padding: 0.25rem 0.65rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03);
  }
  .gsmd-chip small {
    display: block;
    font-size: 0.62rem;
    opacity: 0.75;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }
  .gsmd-chip--gov {
    border-color: rgba(45, 212, 191, 0.35);
    color: var(--accent-ink);
    background: var(--accent-soft);
  }
  .gsmd-chip--fw {
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    padding: 0.15rem 0.5rem;
  }
  .gsmd-chip--sm {
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    padding: 0.12rem 0.5rem;
  }
  .gsmd-arrow {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .gsmd-dna {
    margin: 1.2rem 0 0;
    padding: 0.7rem 1.1rem;
    border: 1px dashed var(--line-strong);
    border-radius: 999px;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    line-height: 1.9;
  }
  .gsmd-dna strong {
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .gsmd-band {
      padding-left: 1.2rem;
      padding-top: 2.4rem;
    }
    .gsmd-cols {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .gsmd-rel {
      white-space: normal;
      text-align: center;
      width: 90%;
    }
    .gsmd-dna {
      border-radius: var(--radius);
    }
  }
</style>
